data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2F2fd89102-b824-4df8-abe9-b9abd3157e9b-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 388px; height: 248px;\" /></p><p>A zwitterion is a compound with no overall electrical charge, but which contains separate parts which are positively and negatively charged.</p><p>Sulphanilic acid exist as dipolar ion (zwitter ion); act as inner salt and ${SO}_{3}H$ group diminishes the basic character of $- {NH}_{2}$.</p>","difficulty":"Easy","source":"BITSAT 2019","_marksId":"64c0e8066f5bfc7ab78ae9ed"},{"id":17291,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"The most reactive amine towards reactions with dil. $HCl$ is","options":["${CH}_{3} - {NH}_{2}$","${( {CH}_{3} )}_{2}NH$","$\\left({CH}_{3}\\right)3 \\cdot N$","${PhNH}_{2}$"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>More be the ability of $N$-atom of $- {NH}_{2}$ group to donate lone pair of electrons to $HCl$ (dil.), more be the reactivity of amine.</p><p>In (B) two alkyl groups are attached to the $- {NH}_{2}$ (having electron releasing nature) which increases the electron donating ability of $N$-atom of $- {NH}_{2}$. In aqueous medium, secondary amine is most basic.& Hence, it& is most reactive. In (D), due to resonance, lone pair of electrons get delocalised and its basic strength is very less.</p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"BITSAT 2017","_marksId":"64c0e7ea6f5bfc7ab78ae8f5"},{"id":17292,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"<p>In the reaction,& </p><p>${CH}_{3} \\cdot {CH}_{2} \\cdot Cl\\overset{KCN}{&#10230;}   \\left(A\\right)$\\overset{LiAlH4}{&#10230;} $\\left(P\\right)$ end product   $\\left(P\\right)$ is</p>","options":["${CH}_{3}{CH}_{2} \\cdot {NO}_{2}$","${CH}_{3}{CH}_{2}{CH}_{2}{NO}_{2}$","${CH}_{3}{CH}_{2}{NH}_{2}$","${CH}_{3} \\cdot {CH}_{2} \\cdot {CH}_{2}{NH}_{2}$"],"answer":3,"solution":"<p>When the reducing agent is lithium aluminium hydride, the aldehyde group is reduced to primary alcohol but the carbon-carbon double bond is unaffected.</p><p>In the given reaction the end product is (d). It is obtained<br />as follows.</p><p>${CH}_{3}{CH}_{2} \\cdot Cl\\overset{KCN}{&#10230;}\\mathop{{CH}_{3}{CH}_{2}CN}_{( A )}\\mathop{&#8594;}_{( Reduction )}^{LiAlH4}{CH}_{3}{CH}_{2}{CH}_{2} \\cdot {NH}_{2}$</p>","difficulty":"Easy","source":"BITSAT 2017","_marksId":"64c0e7ea6f5bfc7ab78ae8fa"},{"id":17293,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"Maximum ${pK}_{b}$& value is of& ","options":["<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fbitsat%252F892301c2-dcab-4ce6-9d04-fd5c95c1f201-image.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=qxfig138\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2F892301c2-dcab-4ce6-9d04-fd5c95c1f201-image.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2F892301c2-dcab-4ce6-9d04-fd5c95c1f201-image.png?alt=media\"><br>","$\\left({CH}_{3}{CH}_{2}\\right)2NH$","$\\left({CH}_{3}\\right)2NH$","<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fbitsat%252F106826dd-1642-402e-80ef-d0ccfd7f88e9-image.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=qxfig138\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2F106826dd-1642-402e-80ef-d0ccfd7f88e9-image.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2F106826dd-1642-402e-80ef-d0cc